sequenceDiagram
  %% Decided by the orchestrator, for Nick's review (2026-11-06): only the Route-publish step of this run holds the Route-serving Nodes, for its seconds, through the Gateway's `route-hold` call; the rest of the run is not held (docs/reference/routes.md#coordinate-publication).
  %% Target design: ADR 0244 task, DECISIONS R2-R4, same shape as cluster.router_set. docs/reference/native-cluster-router.md, docs/cli/cluster.mdx.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten 2026-11-02, rules 1, 22 (no empty DNS note step; cfgmgmt file for the sites).
  %% status: draft
  %% command: cluster:router:unset
  %% kind: cluster.router_unset
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane M icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Current Router<br/>member Node
  participant M as Member Nodes<br/>workloads
  CLI->>GW: cluster:router:unset<br/>CLUSTER
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit cluster:router:unset CLUSTER`
  %%> - syntax: `<cluster> [--force] [--json]`
  %%> Confirmation:
  %%> - without `--force`, the CLI asks first; the default is No; without a terminal, or with `--json`, `--force` is required
  Note over CLI: Inspect Cluster, confirm
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads the Cluster and asks for confirmation; the default is No
  Note over GW: Validate, plan the cleanup<br/>Cluster lock
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - the calling Node has an access grant to a member Node of the Cluster
  %%> - the Cluster is inactive or has no TLD (`cluster.active_router_required`)
  %%> - the Cluster owns no Route (`cluster.routes_require_router`, or `route.reconciliation_required` for an active Route)
  %%> - no other Router change runs for the Cluster; the Gateway waits up to 30 seconds, then refuses with `cluster.router_busy`
  %%> Builds:
  %%> - the Router state to remove: Router sites and certificates, and the LAN rules only the Router needed
  %%> Result:
  %%> - the Router's `router` assignment is recorded as retiring
  %%> - a task is recorded with the full intent
  %%> Decides:
  %%> - whether any Node holds Router state: a Router site, a Router certificate, or a LAN rule only the Router needed
  alt no Node holds Router state
    Note over GW: Clear the Router<br/>R1: no run
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `router` assignment is deleted and the task succeeds at once; no Swamp run starts (R1)
    GW-->>CLI: Router cleared<br/>task succeeded
    %%> What you get:
    %%> - the final result at once; there is nothing to follow
  else Router state on a Node
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-cluster-router
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - starts one Swamp run
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - the state to remove, and the addresses and SSH host keys of the Router and the members
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>task ID
  %%> What you get:
  %%> - the task ID, at once
  %%> Next:
  %%> - the CLI follows the task with `operation:show`
  SW->>GW: Hold the Route Nodes<br/>operation:direct:route-hold
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - asks the Gateway for the hold of each Node that serves the Route's site, for the seconds of this step only, not the whole operation
  %%> - the Gateway reads the Nodes from the admitted intent; the call carries the run ID
  %%> - a Node that another Route write holds is waited for, up to 20 s per call and 2 minutes in all; then the step fails with `route_hold.busy` and the Route step does not run
  %%> - the hold has a 5-minute lease and ends with the Operation, so a lost run cannot keep a Node
  SW->>N: Withdraw the Router sites<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/file · reload
  %%> How:
  %%> - over SSH with `@swamp/ssh` and `@swamp/cfgmgmt/file`; `caddy validate`, then a reload
  %%> No DNS change:
  %%> - an inactive Cluster, or one without a TLD and Routes, gets no Router answers from private DNS
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - removes the Router sites and their certificates, validates the rest, and reloads Caddy; no restart
  %%> - Caddy and the packages stay, as for every role removal that keeps shared packages
  SW->>GW: Release the Route Nodes<br/>operation:direct:route-release
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - gives the Nodes back as soon as the Route step ends, whatever its result; the Route writes that wait for them then start
  %%> - runs beside the next step, so it adds no time
  SW->>M: Remove the LAN rules<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall apply
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - on the Router: removes the 443 and 53 allows for member LAN addresses
  %%> - on each member: removes the allows for the Router's LAN address that no other Route needs
  %%> - never removes WireGuard baseline rules
  SW->>M: Check the rules are gone<br/>@swamp/cfgmgmt/firewall check
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - reads ufw back on every Node and checks the Router lines are absent
  alt every step passes
    M-->>SW: Router lines absent
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the check passed on every Node
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal event
    %%> How the Gateway learns it:
    %%> - its shared run reader sees the terminal event; Swamp never calls the Gateway
    Note over GW: Clear the Router<br/>assignment gone
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `router` assignment is deleted; the Cluster has no Router
    %%> - the task succeeds
  else a step fails
    M--xSW: exit ≠ 0 or line remains
    %%> When:
    %%> - Caddy refuses the config, SSH fails, or a rule is still present
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code, failed step
    %%> The Gateway reads:
    %%> - which step failed and its error code
    Note over GW: Keep the assignment<br/>failed · rerun after a fix
    %%> Result:
    %%> - the `router` assignment stays, marked failed
    %%> - the task fails
    %%> On the Node:
    %%> - steps that finished stay done; there is no rollback, because the Cluster serves no traffic through the Router
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - run the same command again; it skips what is already removed
  end
  loop every 2 s until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - asks for the task's status every 2 seconds until it has ended
    GW-->>CLI: status + result
    %%> Returns:
    %%> - the current status, and the result once the task has ended
  end
  end
